===============================================================================
Third-party data in lib/data-in.js
===============================================================================

lib/data-in.js holds a small, hand-curated subset of two public Indian
reference datasets: 242 pincodes (with post office, district and locality)
and 820 IFSC codes (with branch name and MICR code) for 43 cities. Both were
fetched on 2026-10-19. The licence facts below were checked online on
2026-10-19; what was and was not verified is stated for each.


1. All India Pincode Directory (India Post)
-------------------------------------------

Provider:  Department of Posts, Ministry of Communications, Government of India
Source:    Open Government Data (OGD) Platform India
           https://www.data.gov.in/catalog/all-india-pincode-directory
           https://www.data.gov.in/resource/all-india-pincode-directory-till-last-month
Used:      pincode, post office name and district of selected offices, and
           the locality each office serves.
Licence:   Government Open Data License - India (GODL-India)
           https://www.data.gov.in/Godl
           Gazette of India, Extraordinary, Part I Section 1, No. 42,
           13 February 2017:
           https://www.data.gov.in/sites/default/files/Gazette_Notification_OGDL.pdf

Verified:
  - The footer of the OGD Platform's pages, including the catalog and
    resource pages above, states: "Content is owned by the respective Ministries/Departments/
    Organizations and licensed under the Government Open Data License-India."
  - The resource page's own licence field is empty, so that platform-wide
    statement is the licence that applies to this dataset.
  - The gazette text of GODL-India grants "a worldwide, royalty-free,
    non-exclusive license to use, adapt, publish (either in original, or in
    adapted and/or derivative forms), translate, display, add value, and
    create derivative works (including products and services), for all
    lawful commercial and non-commercial purposes". Section 4(a) requires
    users to "acknowledge the provider, source, and license of data by
    explicitly publishing the attribution statement", including the URL of
    the data. Section 4(c) says users must not suggest that the data
    provider endorses their use.
Not verified:
  - The exact wording of the attribution template in section 5 of the
    gazette could not be read from the PDF. The statement below names the
    provider, source, licence and URL, as section 4(a) requires.

Attribution statement:
  Contains pincode data from the All India Pincode Directory, published by
  the Department of Posts, Ministry of Communications, Government of India,
  on the Open Government Data Platform India
  (https://www.data.gov.in/catalog/all-india-pincode-directory) under the
  Government Open Data License - India (https://www.data.gov.in/Godl).

